---
import { SITE_CONFIG } from "@/data/site"
---

<article
  class="flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-8 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 md:flex-row"
>
  <div
    class="[&>p]:mb-4 [&>p>strong]:text-yellow-500 dark:[&>p>strong]:text-yellow-100 [&>p>strong]:font-normal [&>p>strong]:font-mono text-pretty order-2 md:order-1"
  >
    <p>
      I'm a Software Engineer who enjoys owning the whole problem—from
      understanding a workflow to shaping the architecture, shipping the
      interface, and proving that the result behaves correctly. I build
      <strong
        >web products, backend systems, data platforms, and automation tools</strong
      > for different domains rather than limiting myself to one framework or one
      type of application.
    </p>

    <p>
      That range is deliberate. A healthcare platform taught me to think in
      secure domain boundaries; a reminder product pushed me toward durable,
      retry-safe processing; a terminal data platform sharpened my approach to
      <strong>quality, reconciliation, and reproducibility</strong>; and a
      local-first security app made recovery and key-management constraints
      impossible to ignore.
    </p>

    <p>
      Across languages and contexts, my approach stays consistent:
      <strong
        >make boundaries explicit, automate the risky paths, test real behavior,
        and keep the product useful for the person operating it</strong
      >. I’m interested in software-engineering roles and client work where that
      combination of breadth and engineering discipline creates practical value.
    </p>
  </div>

  <img
    width="200"
    height="200"
    src={SITE_CONFIG.aboutImage}
    alt="Ali Hamdaoui attending an engineering conference in Morocco"
    class="order-1 h-80 w-64 object-cover p-1 md:order-2 rotate-3 lg:p-2 lg:w-64 rounded-2xl bg-black/20 dark:bg-yellow-500/5 ring-1 ring-black/70 dark:ring-white/20"
    style="object-position: 50% 35%"
  />
</article>
